All 5 streams contributed. 37 total findings. No contradictions. Here's the distilled answer:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Root Cause (the delete→import cycle problem)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mgenanki.Note[0m generates a GUID from a hash of [1mall fields[22m. When any field content changes (you edit the card), the GUID changes on the next build, so Anki sees it as a [1mnew note[22m and creates a duplicate instead of updating. That's the entire reason for the current manual delete cycle.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### The Fix (one class, ~5 lines)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mpython
[0m[38;5;10m# koine-anki/shared/stable_note.py
import genanki

class StableNote(genanki.Note):
    def __init__(self, *args, identity_key: str, **kwargs):
        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)
        self._identity_key = identity_key

    @property
    def guid(self):
        return genanki.guid_for(self._identity_key)
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Then in [38;5;10mgen_all_decks.py[0m, [38;5;10mcompounds/generate_deck.py[0m, and [38;5;10mkoine-pimsleur/src/generate_decks.py[0m, change every [38;5;10mgenanki.Note(...)[0m to:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mpython
[0m[38;5;10m# Identity key = anything that won't change even if the card content is edited
StableNote(model=model, fields=[front, back],
           identity_key=f"{deck_id}:{verb_key}:{form_idx}")
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
After this fix, running [38;5;10mdeploy.py[0m twice in a row will UPDATE existing cards (preserving all your review history/scheduling) instead of duplicating them.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Architecture Answer[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The existing [38;5;10mgenanki → .apkg → importPackage[0m pipeline is the correct architecture. No need to switch to direct SQLite (risky, locked while Anki runs) or build a complex API. If you want programmatic triggering (e.g., from an agent), a 30-line FastAPI wrapper over AnkiConnect is all that's needed. Full blueprint is in [38;5;10mrecommendations.md[0m]9;Response complete.[0m[0m[38;5;12m[1m✓ Created checkpoint 1

